{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"EXT_ID:697765 AND SRC:MED","internalQuery":"EXT_ID:697765 AND SRC:MED","resultType":"CORE","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"697765","source":"MED","pmid":"697765","pmcid":"PMC1185887","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC1185887"]},"doi":"10.1042/bj1740073","title":"Chemical structure and biodegradability of halogenated aromatic compounds. Two catechol 1,2-dioxygenases from a 3-chlorobenzoate-grown pseudomonad.","authorString":"Dorn E, Knackmuss HJ.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Dorn E","lastName":"Dorn","firstName":"E","initials":"E"},{"fullName":"Knackmuss HJ","lastName":"Knackmuss","firstName":"H J","initials":"HJ"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["wikipedia"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"1","volume":"174","journalIssueId":117649,"dateOfPublication":"1978 Jul","monthOfPublication":7,"yearOfPublication":1978,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Biochem J","title":"The Biochemical journal","essn":"1470-8728","issn":"0264-6021","isoabbreviation":"Biochem J","nlmid":"2984726R"},"printPublicationDate":"1978-07-01"},"pubYear":"1978","pageInfo":"73-84","abstractText":"1. Two catechol 1,2-dioxygenases, pyrocatechase I and pyrocatechase II, were found in 3-chlorobenzoate-grown cells of Pseudomonas sp. B 13. The latter enzyme showed high relative activities with 3- and 4-chlorocatechol compared with catechol. 2. In benzoate-grown cells, only pyrocatechase I was induced. It was purified 29-fold with a final specific activity of 20 mumol of catechol oxygenated/min per mg of protein and an overall yield of 22%. Because of the instability of pyrocatechase II on chromatography and dialysis, no increase of specific activity was obtained during the purification experiments. 3. Molecular weights of pyrocatechase I and pyrocatechase II were 82000 and 67000 respectively. 4. For both pyrocatechases the pH optimum was found to be at 8.0.5. Inhibitions of the two pyrocatechases by Cu2+ and Hg2+ ions and p-chloromercuribenzoate were different. The effect on pyrocatechase I after incubation for 20 h with the heavy metals was decreased by addition of 1 mM-2-mercaptoethanol to the reaction mixture. The inhibition of pyrocatechase II was even enhanced under these conditions. 6. Extradiol cleavage of 3-methylcatechol in addition to intradiol fission at a ratio of 1:14 was observed only with pyrocatechase I.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["research-article","Journal Article"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Pseudomonas","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"EN","qualifierName":"enzymology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Cations, Divalent","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"PD","qualifierName":"pharmacology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Benzoates","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Chlorobenzoates","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Catechols"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Isomerases","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Oxygenases","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"IP","qualifierName":"isolation & purification"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Chemistry"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Molecular Weight"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Biodegradation, Environmental"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Chemical Phenomena"}]},"chemicalList":{"chem